                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Cornelia</forename>
                        <surname>Newton</surname>
                        <addName>née Collins</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1816-09-02"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Wife of John Frank <persName key="NEW01">Newton</persName>; sister of Harriet Boinville and daughter of John Collins. The editors of Mary Shelley's 
    <title>Journal</title> have Cornelia as the sister of Mrs Boinville (not to be confused with Cornelia Boinville, the Boinville's daughter who married Thomas Turner and was 
    at risk to Shelley at one point) and the wife of John Frank Newton. Entries for 'Newtons' include Mrs Newton.</p>
                        <p>Godwin notes her death.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"><title>The Journals of Mary Shelley</title> ed Feldman and Scott-Kilvert (John Hopkins, Baltimore, 1987)  </bibl>
                </person>
